<title>GREECE: XIOSBANK SAYS H1 BUSINESS LOANS UP 37PCT.</title>
<headline>XIOSBANK SAYS H1 BUSINESS LOANS UP 37PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Xiosbank said its corporate loans grew 37 percent in the first half, exceeding its budgeted goal for 1997. The balance of outstanding corporate credit stood at 49.78 billion drachmas.</p>
<p>Xiosbank's base business loan rate for this week will stay unchanged at 17.50 percent.</p>
<p>Its Xios-Alma savings account offers a gross annual return of 9.92 percent with monthly interest payments.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
